{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:854601d558724c0b","name":"Rock Slide","source":{"id":"source:reference-854601d558724c0b","title":"Rock Slide","revision":21423,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:46:30Z","sha256":"18c8ac952dac7cb5292bc721be0e7ec852e82de54c21a311a3b9b8fc451fbe01","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21423","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Rock%20Slide&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-854601d558724c0b","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["A large mass of rocks and boulders tumbles down the mountainside toward you."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Rock Slides can be particularly dangerous to a group of heroes. Their enemies can start a Rock Slide intentionally and perhaps even direct its path by placing artificial structures to funnel the rocks or by using ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," to move boulders onto a desired course. In addition, you can use a Rock Slide to steer heroes in a particular direction.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Rock Slide Statistics (CL 9)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Keywords:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Artificial"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Artificial"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Natural"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Natural"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trigger:"]}," A loud noise occurs within the area of the Hazard; targeting every being and object in the area.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Attack:"]}," +11 vs ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 2d12+1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Recurrence:"]}," Each round at the start of the target's turn, as long as the target remains within the area of the Rock Slide.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"},":"]}," The following are suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"}," for this Hazard:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knowledge (Physical Sciences)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knowledge_(Physical_Sciences)"}," (DC 23):"]}," The character determines from the surroundings that the area might be unstable. A minor seismic quake, a shot from a blaster bolt, or an explosive could cause a Rock Slide."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Survival"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Survival","referenceId":"reference:8302496de0ace160"}," (DC 28):"]}," After observing the area, the character finds a few places where he or she could take cover during a Rock Slide, gaining a +5 circumstance bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," against the Hazard."]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
